{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.magnitude_change_forces_nonuniform_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.magnitude_change_forces_nonuniform_weight","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L212-L231","doc":"**Contrapositive — a magnitude change forces a non-uniform weight.**\n\nIf a weighted block readout differs from the scalar trace, then some per-block\nweight is `≠ 1`. The operator-valued combiner alone (`w ≡ 1`) can never do it;\nthe missing `1.585×` requires a genuine `Δ_λ`-type per-partition weight — a\ndifferent functional than the trace, and (per the `Δ_λ` gate) one that may only\nbe *derived*, never fitted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedReadout_eq_of_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedReadout_eq_of_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L193-L210","doc":"Uniform per-block weights (`w ≡ 1`) recover the scalar trace: no magnitude\nchange. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedReadout_sub_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedReadout_sub_trace","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L170-L191","doc":"**The deviation of a weighted readout is carried entirely by the weight.**\n\n  `(Σ i, w i · τ (P i·X·P i)) − τ X = Σ i, (w i − 1) · τ (P i·X·P i)`.\n\nThe right-hand side is `0` when every `w i = 1`; a magnitude change is possible\n*only* through a non-uniform per-block weight. This is the \"by how much\" answer:\nthe operator structure contributes nothing on its own — all of `μ₃ − c₃` must\nlive in a per-block weight `w i ≠ 1` (the `Δ_λ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.operatorCombiner_eq_scalarTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.operatorCombiner_eq_scalarTrace","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L150-L168","doc":"**ROUTE 1 conclusion — the operator combiner supplies zero extra magnitude.**\n\nThe block-resolved readout of the operator-valued combiner equals the scalar\nMarkov trace exactly:\n\n  `operatorCombinerReadout τ P X = τ X`.\n\nHence keeping the operator (matrix) structure through the branching multiplies\nthe scalar trace by a factor of **exactly `1`**: it reproduces `c₃`, never `μ₃`,\nand supplies `0` of the missing `r* − 1 ≈ 0.585`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedBlockReadout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.weightedBlockReadout","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L143-L148","doc":"A general **weighted** block readout with per-block weight `w i : R` — the\nshape any `Δ_λ`-type per-partition weight would take. `w ≡ 1` recovers the plain\noperator-combiner readout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.operatorCombinerReadout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.operatorCombinerReadout","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L136-L141","doc":"The observable read off the operator-valued branching combiner: the sum of\nthe diagonal per-block trace compressions `τ (P i · X · P i)`. This is the\n\"keep the matrix structure, then close the trace\" readout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.trace_partition_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.trace_partition_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/A3OperatorCombinerMagnitude.lean#L90-L134","doc":"**Partition-of-unity trace collapse (the cited invariant).**\n\nLet `{P i}` be an orthogonal resolution of unity in `A` (`P i · P j = 0` for\n`i ≠ j`, `Σ i, P i = 1`), and let `τ : A →+ R` be cyclic. Then the trace of any\n`X` equals the sum of its diagonal block compressions:\n\n  `τ X = Σ i, τ (P i · X · P i)`.\n\nOff-diagonal blocks vanish under the cyclic trace; the per-block weight is\nidentically `1`. This is the `W = β = 1` specialisation of the interface-operator\nblock-diagonality, isolated here as the magnitude invariant for ROUTE 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}